---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Adam Sneed: security-focused engineering leader with a two-decade track record in operations, privileged access, and agentic AI systems."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pb-20 pt-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div data-reveal>
        <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-textMuted">About</span>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-balance text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-textMain md:text-6xl">Engineering every layer</h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bio -->
  <section class="px-6 pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="100">
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-textMuted">
          <p class="text-pretty text-xl leading-relaxed text-textMain">
            Two decades building from the physical layer up &mdash; RedHat and AIX administration, datacenter operations, enterprise networking, all the way through security engineering and now autonomous AI agents.
          </p>
          <p class="text-pretty">
            At Netwrix, I&apos;m a Senior Solutions Architect in Professional Services &mdash; the subject matter expert on our PAM product. I design and deploy enterprise PAM solutions, build automation frameworks, and translate complex security requirements into production-grade implementations.
          </p>
          <p class="text-pretty">
            Outside of that, I engineer across all three layers.
            <span class="font-medium text-textMain">Physical:</span> home lab infrastructure, edge devices, custom hardware rigs.
            <span class="font-medium text-textMain">Software:</span> APIs, integration pipelines, automation systems that hold under pressure.
            <span class="font-medium text-textMain">Agentic:</span> multi-agent orchestration, prompt engineering, and autonomous workflows built with the same discipline I bring to privileged access &mdash; least privilege, human oversight, audit trails, fail-safe defaults.
          </p>
          <p class="text-pretty">
            Each layer informs the next. Infrastructure discipline shapes software design. Software discipline shapes agent design. That&apos;s the through-line.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Operating Principles -->
  <section class="px-6 pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="150">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-2xl font-bold text-textMain md:text-3xl">Operating Principles</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-4">
          <li class="group flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="mt-0.5 flex h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-accent/10">
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-accent">01</span>
            </span>
            <span class="text-lg text-textMuted transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:text-textMain">Build for production, not demos.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="group flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="mt-0.5 flex h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-accent/10">
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-accent">02</span>
            </span>
            <span class="text-lg text-textMuted transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:text-textMain">Security is architecture, not a feature.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="group flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="mt-0.5 flex h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-accent/10">
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-accent">03</span>
            </span>
            <span class="text-lg text-textMuted transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:text-textMain">Agents need guardrails.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="group flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="mt-0.5 flex h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-accent/10">
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-accent">04</span>
            </span>
            <span class="text-lg text-textMuted transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:text-textMain">Write it down.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Policy Lens -->
  <section class="px-6 pb-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="200">
        <div class="border-l-2 border-accent/30 pl-6">
          <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-textMain md:text-3xl">Policy Lens</h2>
          <p class="text-pretty text-lg leading-relaxed text-textMuted">
            My Juris Doctor from LSU Law informs how I design policies, evaluate regulatory risk, and write statement-of-work scope with contract-level precision.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
